In article <1992Sep17.225646.18591@bmers95.bnr.ca> nelling@bnr.ca (Peter
Snelling) writes:
>Brand new suggestion for nethack:  The ability to set a
>monster_confirm option string.  I would set it to "ebjvF".
>Then, before I attacked any e, b, j, v, or F, I would get
>a message "WARNING -- Really Attack? [yn]"

Well, I'm afraid that's a bit beyond my hack hacking abilities, but
having just lost 2 (*two!* - count 'em) consecutive promising wizards to
floating eyes I had to do something about it.

The appended patch changes the direction keys to mean "move in this
direction, unless you can see there's a monster in the way" (like the
shifted direction keys, but you only go one square).  The traditional
meaning of the keys ("move/attack") you get by CTRL-direction.

It doesn't work with the numberpad option (sorry).

Enjoy.

*** cmd.c.orig	Thu May 31 05:31:25 1990
--- cmd.c	Thu Sep 24 17:28:32 1992
***************
*** 728,736 ****
--- 728,743 ----
  	if(movecmd(*cmd)) {
  	walk:
  		if(multi) flags.mv = 1;
+ 		flags.run = 4;
  		domove();
+ 		flags.run = 0;
  		return;
  	}
+ 	if(movecmd(unctrl(*cmd))) {
+ 		if(multi) flags.mv = 1;
+ 		domove();
+ 		return;
+ 	}
  	if(movecmd(flags.num_pad ? unmeta(*cmd) : lowc(*cmd))) {
  		flags.run = 1;
  	rush:
